breeze-grub (5.17.5-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Team upload.
  * Upload to unstable.
  * Remove the postinst/prerm scripts that set breeze as default GRUB 2 theme
    in /etc/default/grub: other than being fragile, it is not expected that
    just installing a theme will change the default without the explicit choice
    of the user.
  * Restrict the architecture to the ones where GRUB 2 is available; copy the
    comment & architecture list from grub-theme-starfield (provided by
    src:grub2).
  * Small changes to the description.
  * Install in /usr/share/grub/themes/ rather than /boot/grub/themes/, just
    like other themes.

 -- Pino Toscano <pino@debian.org>  Fri, 17 Jan 2020 00:19:10 +0100

